{
    "background_story": "Kolton was a skilled architect with a passion for sustainable design. Growing up in a small desert town, he learned to appreciate the importance of harnessing the sun's energy. After completing his studies, Kolton set out to create homes that not only minimized environmental impact but also maximized the use of natural light. His breakthrough design, dubbed the 'Suntrap,' became an instant sensation. By carefully orienting the building's layout and incorporating specialized materials, Kolton's Suntrap homes could absorb and store solar energy, providing warmth and light even on the coldest winter nights. His innovative design earned him international recognition, and soon, people from all over the world were seeking out his expertise to build their own sun-kissed sanctuaries.",
